  "analysis": "The ELF loader loads sections by name (.text, .data, .rodata) using section headers, not program headers. It reads 32-bit little-endian words from each section and stores them at their virtual address in the VM memory object. This confirms mipsel little-endian is correct and the binary must have proper section headers. I need to see the rest of the loader to understand entry point selection.",
  "plan": "Inspect the rest of the ELF loader (lines 1780-1850) to understand how the entry point is determined and whether symbols matter.",
